# squads/<squad-id>.md template (design 5.9)
#
# One file per squad, named after the squad's id (for example
# squads/security-hardening.md). Updated on every status change by the
# squad's own session/lead — "The squad's own file; updated on every status
# change". Claims here are information only (C2): they tell other sessions
# what is in flight, they never block anyone; only HOLDS.md and
# LANDING-LOCK are mechanically enforced (by the pre-push hook).
#
# Row format (one line — the design calls this "one squad's row"):
#
#   squad=<squad-id> | session=<session-id-or-in-session> | lead=<role> | worktree=<absolute-path> | branch=<branch-name> | claim=<trees-or-files> | status=<planned|in-flight|gated|handed-back|waiting-for-founder|landed|blocked|released> | last-updated=<ISO8601> by <who>
#
# scripts/dev-machine-capacity.sh counts active dispatches by grepping this
# directory for "status=in-flight" — keep the field name and value exactly
# as shown (case-sensitive, no extra spaces around "=") or the capacity
# monitor will undercount.
#
# A pending landing announcement is appended below the row as a second line
# (design: "The row also carries the squad's landing announcements when one
# is pending") and removed once the landing lock is released and the
# landing is posted to LANDING-LOG.md:
#
#   LANDING-ANNOUNCEMENT squad=<squad-id> branch=<branch-name> announced-at=<ISO8601> by=<who>
#
# A row untouched for 2 hours with no live session behind it is "stale"
# (G3) — the chief asks the founder before releasing or re-assigning it.
#
# Example (illustration only — replace <squad-id> in the filename and every
# field below):
# squad=security-hardening | session=separate-session-2 | lead=security-lead | worktree=/Users/danielpiatkowski/AI-Agent-Workspace/omnipus/wt-security-hardening | branch=feature/security-hardening | claim=pkg/auth/, pkg/fspolicy/ | status=in-flight | last-updated=2026-09-25T09:05:00Z by security-lead
